{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert-identification","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert-identification","kind":"remark","title":"Third-generation meson ratio: value at $q_0$ and identification with $\\phi(1020)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert","tags":["meson","phi-1020","comparison-with-measurement"],"text":"gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert-identification.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert-identification\"></a><p>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code> the <a href=\"#prop:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mass-physical-face\">third-generation ratio</a> evaluates to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q_0^7 - q_0^{-7})\\cdot(15/7)^2 \\approx 7.320</code>.</p>\n<p>The predicted ratio identifies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> as the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\phi(1020)</code> meson. The odd-torus tower corresponds exactly to the strange-vector meson sequence. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\eta</code> meson carries an axial-anomaly contribution and falls outside this single-torus model.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert-identification.md","heading":"Remark","number":"13.37.10","page":"b/rem-gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert-identification"}
